---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — Loop"
  description="Placeholder privacy policy. Replace before launch."
>
  <section class="bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pt-16 pb-24 md:pt-20">
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-950">Privacy policy</h1>

      <div class="mt-10 rounded-xl border-2 border-zinc-950 bg-white p-6 md:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-950">Placeholder. Replace this page before launch.</h2>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-zinc-700 leading-relaxed">
          <p>
            This page intentionally has no policy text. The starter ships without one because legal language has to be specific to your company, product, jurisdiction, and what data you actually collect.
          </p>
          <p>
            The <a href="/demo" class="font-medium text-zinc-950 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-zinc-600">demo form</a> on this site collects names and emails. As soon as that form is wired up to real visitors, you need a real privacy policy here.
          </p>
          <p>Three ways to handle it:</p>
          <ul class="space-y-3 pl-4">
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-zinc-400" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span>
                Use a generator service. <a href="https://termly.io" class="font-medium text-zinc-950 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-zinc-600">Termly</a>, <a href="https://iubenda.com" class="font-medium text-zinc-950 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-zinc-600">Iubenda</a>, and <a href="https://getterms.io" class="font-medium text-zinc-950 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-zinc-600">GetTerms</a> all produce customized policies and update them when laws change. Most cost $10–30 per month.
              </span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-zinc-400" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span>Hire a startup lawyer to write one. Usually the right call once you are charging real customers.</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-zinc-400" aria-hidden="true"></span>
              <span>Adapt a public template you trust and have a lawyer review it. Slower, but free.</span>
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            When you have the real content, replace everything inside <code class="rounded bg-zinc-100 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-sm font-mono">src/pages/privacy.astro</code> with your policy. The footer link will keep working.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
